WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.760
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.910
Many of you have surely heard the word Animoji,
which refers to these emoji figures that are

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.750
animated in real time and react to our facial
gestures.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:19.500
This is implemented in the new iPhone X phones,
however, to accomplish this, it uses a dot

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.180
projector get a good enough understanding
of the geometry of the human face.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.980
So, how about a technique that doesn't need
any specialized gear, takes not even a video

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.949
of you, but one photograph as an input, and
creates a digital avatar of us that can be

00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:36.929
animated in real time.

00:00:36.929 --> 00:00:38.879
Well, sign me up!

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:40.940
Have a look at these incredible results.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:47.829
As you can see, the final result also includes
secondary components like eyes, teeth, tongue,

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:48.829
and gum.

00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:53.940
Now, these avatars don't have to be fully
photorealistic, but have to capture the appearance

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.859
and gestures of the user well enough so they
can be used in video games or any telepresence

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:04.059
application where a set of users interact
in a virtual world.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:08.840
As opposed to many prior works, the hair is
not reconstructed strand by strand, because

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.140
doing this in real time is not feasible.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:16.190
Also, note that the information we are given
is highly incomplete, because the backside

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:21.510
of the head is not captured, but these characters
also have a quite appropriate looking hairstyle

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:22.510
there.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.460
So, how is this even possible?

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:29.920
Well, first, the input image is segmented
into the face part and the hair part.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.270
Then, the hair part is run through a neural
network that tries to extract attributes like

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:40.840
length, spikiness, are there hair buns, is
there a ponytail, where the hairline is, and

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.840
more.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:47.909
This is an extremely deep neural network with
over 50 layers and it took 40 thousand images

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:49.700
of different hairstyles to train.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.680
Now, since it is highly unlikely that the
input photo shows someone with a hairstyle

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:00.520
that was never ever worn by anyone else, we
can look into a big dataset of already existing

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.210
hairstyles and choose the closest one that
fits the attributes extracted by the neural

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.210
network.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.909
Such a smart idea, loving it.

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:13.939
You can see how well this works in practice,
and in the next step, the movement and appearance

00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:19.709
of the final hair geometry can be computed
in real time through a novel polygonal strip

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:20.769
representation.

00:02:20.769 --> 00:02:25.469
The technique also supports retargeting, which
means that our gestures can be transferred

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:27.219
to different characters.

00:02:27.219 --> 00:02:32.209
The framework is also very robust to different
lighting conditions, which means that a differently

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:35.790
lit photograph will lead to very similar outputs.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.900
The same applies for expressions.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:42.379
This is one of those highly desirable details
that makes or breaks the usability of a new

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:47.709
technique in production environments, and
this one passed with flying colors.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:52.170
In these comparisons, you can also see that
the quality of the results also smokes the

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.170
competition.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:57.749
A variant of the technology can be downloaded
through the link in the video description.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.760
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

